The '''Storming of the Baliscan Cabildo''' ({{lang-bl|Assalto al Cabildo Baliscano}}), also known as the '''Castejónazo''' (from "Castejón" and the [[W:Spanish nouns#Other suffixes|''-azo'' suffix]] of violent augmentation) occurred on 21 April 1918, when around 500 rebelling soldiers and other [[Baliscan Revolution|revolutionaries]] stormed and subsequently occupied the [[Old Baliscan Cabildo|Baliscan Cabildo]] in reaction to increasingly violent repression by the state.

The coup and subsequent siege of the Cabildo was a significant development in the revolution, and marked the beginning of the [[Tragic Week]], a period of increasingly violent confrontation between varying left and right-wing factions in the unrest as military loyalty to the administration of [[Máximo Burjassot]] administration collapsed.{{Balisca articles}}
